  "id": "inborn-error-of-metabolism",
  "term": "inborn error of metabolism",
  "definition": "An inborn error of metabolism is a disorder present from birth in which a genetic change disrupts a normal metabolic process, often because an enzyme is faulty or unstable. In the example described here, cystathionine beta-synthase deficiency causes homocysteine to build up and can be associated with learning and behavioral problems.",
